    Old network gear — routers, switches, wireless access points, firewalls, structured cabling — accumulates in server rooms, IT store cupboards and network cabinets long after it's been replaced. This page covers what's accepted, why enterprise switches sometimes carry configuration data that's worth flagging, and how bulk network-refresh pickups are planned.
  </p>

